Un faux site pourrait copier ces pages — mais il porterait un autre sceau. Le sceau canonique affiché par cette page est ancré hors d’elle : dans les captures de la Wayback Machine et dans les preuves Bitcoin/OpenTimestamps. Compare : Lis le sceau canonique affiché sur cette page (accueil et panneau Preuves). Ouvre une capture Wayback du site (les horodatages sont listés au panneau Preuves, section §F) et lis le sceau que la page capturée affiche : pour la même version, c’est le même sceau — l’Archive n’est pas à nous pour la réécrire. Pour les états du dossier, suis les chemins OpenTimestamps et RFC 3161 de la même section : l’empreinte existait à cette date, dans une chaîne que nous ne contrôlons pas. Une page dont le sceau ne correspond à aucun de ses ancrages n’est pas ce site, quoi qu’elle prétende. Ouvrir le panneau Preuves et ancrages","mots":["41","verifie","que","c","est","bien","nous","le","sceau","contre","les","ancrages","externes","un","faux","site","pourrait","copier","ces","pages","mais","il","porterait","un","autre","sceau","le","sceau","canonique","affiche","par","cette","page","est","ancre","hors","d","elle","dans","les","captures","de","la","wayback","machine","et","dans","les","preuves","bitcoin","opentimestamps","compare","lis","le","sceau","canonique","affiche","sur","cette","page","accueil","et","panneau","preuves","ouvre","une","capture","wayback","du","site","les","horodatages","sont","listes","au","panneau","preuves","section","f","et","lis","le","sceau","que","la","page","capturee","affiche","pour","la","meme","version","c","est","le","meme","sceau","l","archive","n","est","pas","a","nous","pour","la","reecrire","pour","les","etats","du","dossier","suis","les","chemins","opentimestamps","et","rfc","3161","de","la","meme","section","l","empreinte","existait","a","cette","date","dans","une","chaine","que","nous","ne","controlons","pas","une","page","dont","le","sceau","ne","correspond","a","aucun","de","ses","ancrages","n","est","pas","ce","site","quoi","qu","elle","pretende","ouvrir","le","panneau","preuves","et","ancrages"],"empreinte":"37b3b5a2135ad034d7a3ba54b4cd9e20ac37bcaaa5b85f531af46dc993f4dee6","merkle":{"feuille":164,"chemin":[{"cote":"droite","digest":"e52abc366cd69aee6390d6697f5f5ed5bfc298e8eb38b1cc93d3afede78a7323"},{"cote":"droite","digest":"aaf1cdcc9001e81f81012340539c2ca334e88b1f69910a44027342e961c025b1"},{"cote":"gauche","digest":"28e127a71da2651f3f5194f9f29e8af17404ffb98edd928007e2e75520fc1473"},{"cote":"droite","digest":"2dcf1cf2891bd42cbe2ce49b78d962a996473737c0415fb6b65b15618afe4b54"},{"cote":"droite","digest":"4acf95756dc50b307b1efe3898b933a1db0eb2acc634626b03c66fd31f4d4830"},{"cote":"gauche","digest":"cd8f0b5a9f787cccfd49de8804f2a519b0f6ce91b845b7380fa73ac26941cff0"},{"cote":"droite","digest":"61783b3d0e30b8ee5d94f4bc62cd810067545dfb8758b360571efe39278cbf9c"},{"cote":"gauche","digest":"35bb3360f798e767433de9562880ae5e4200860cfb53e7f05339aebfec315905"}]}},{"id":165,"page":"exposition.html","ancre":"presence","titre":"Preuve de présence consentie — déclarée, jamais captée [forme bornée]","panneau":"Ton exposition","texte":"42 Preuve de présence consentie — déclarée, jamais captée [forme bornée] Exploratoire, dans sa forme bornée : une présence sur ce site n’est jamais captée — aucune géolocalisation n’est demandée, aucune n’est lue. Ce que tu peux faire, c’est déclarer toi-même une présence, et sceller la déclaration par l’atome-décision : ta parole, datée, dans ta propre chaîne, que le site ne peut pas vérifier et ne prétend pas vérifier. Sa valeur est exactement celle d’une déclaration scellée : la tienne. Le lieu que tu déclares (dans tes mots) Contexte (pourquoi cette déclaration compte pour toi) Sceller cette déclaration","mots":["42","preuve","de","presence","consentie","declaree","jamais","captee","forme","bornee","exploratoire","dans","sa","forme","bornee","une","presence","sur","ce","site","n","est","jamais","captee","aucune","geolocalisation","n","est","demandee","aucune","n","est","lue","ce","que","tu","peux","faire","c","est","declarer","toi-meme","une","presence","et","sceller","la","declaration","par","l","atome-decision","ta","parole","datee","dans","ta","propre","chaine","que","le","site","ne","peut","pas","verifier","et","ne","pretend","pas","verifier","sa","valeur","est","exactement","celle","d","une","declaration","scellee","la","tienne","le","lieu","que","tu","declares","dans","tes","mots","contexte","pourquoi","cette","declaration","compte","pour","toi","sceller","cette","declaration"],"empreinte":"e52abc366cd69aee6390d6697f5f5ed5bfc298e8eb38b1cc93d3afede78a7323","merkle":{"feuille":165,"chemin":[{"cote":"gauche","digest":"37b3b5a2135ad034d7a3ba54b4cd9e20ac37bcaaa5b85f531af46dc993f4dee6"},{"cote":"droite","digest":"aaf1cdcc9001e81f81012340539c2ca334e88b1f69910a44027342e961c025b1"},{"cote":"gauche","digest":"28e127a71da2651f3f5194f9f29e8af17404ffb98edd928007e2e75520fc1473"},{"cote":"droite","digest":"2dcf1cf2891bd42cbe2ce49b78d962a996473737c0415fb6b65b15618afe4b54"},{"cote":"droite","digest":"4acf95756dc50b307b1efe3898b933a1db0eb2acc634626b03c66fd31f4d4830"},{"cote":"gauche","digest":"cd8f0b5a9f787cccfd49de8804f2a519b0f6ce91b845b7380fa73ac26941cff0"},{"cote":"droite","digest":"61783b3d0e30b8ee5d94f4bc62cd810067545dfb8758b360571efe39278cbf9c"},{"cote":"gauche","digest":"35bb3360f798e767433de9562880ae5e4200860cfb53e7f05339aebfec315905"}]}},{"id":166,"page":"exposition.html","ancre":"telephone-soir","titre":"Ce que ton téléphone raconte ce soir — lis le rapport de confidentialité de ton propre système","panneau":"Ton exposition","texte":"46 Ce que ton téléphone raconte ce soir — lis le rapport de confidentialité de ton propre système Ton téléphone tient déjà le journal : quelles applications ont touché ta localisation, ta caméra ou ton micro, et quels domaines réseau elles ont contactés. Il suffit de l’activer et de le lire. Ce guide parcourt les deux systèmes, depuis les pages officielles des fabricants ; chaque étape se scelle dans ton cerveau. iPhone — Rapport de confidentialité des apps (iOS 15.2 et suivants) 1. Active-le. Réglages → Confidentialité et sécurité → Rapport de confidentialité des apps → Activer. Il ne commence à recueillir qu’à partir de ce moment — laisse-lui quelques jours d’usage normal avant de juger. Ses données sont chiffrées et gardées seulement sur ton appareil ; le désactiver les efface. Sceller cette étape 2. Lis les accès aux capteurs. Le rapport montre combien de fois — et quand — chaque application a accédé à des données sensibles ou à des capteurs (localisation, caméra, micro, contacts, photos) au cours des 7 derniers jours. Une application qui lit ta localisation la nuit, inutilisée, est un fait sur lequel agir. Sceller cette étape 3. Lis l’activité réseau. Le rapport liste aussi les domaines contactés par les applications — y compris les domaines de pisteurs tiers qu’une application ne nomme jamais. Un domaine inconnu, contacté souvent, est le cousin de la couche proximité : renseigne-toi avant de faire confiance à l’application. Sceller cette étape 4. Révoque l’excès. Le rapport ne bloque rien — il te dit où regarder. Les interrupteurs sont dans Réglages → Confidentialité et sécurité, capteur par capteur : Jamais, ou Demander la prochaine fois. Révoquer est une décision : scelle-la comme telle (section §A de ton dossier de suivi). Sceller cette étape Source officielle — Apple Support, À propos du Rapport de confidentialité des apps Android — Tableau de bord Confidentialité (Android 12 et suivants) 1. Ouvre-le. Paramètres → Sécurité et confidentialité (ou Confidentialité) → Tableau de bord Confidentialité. Il montre quelles applications ont accédé à quelles autorisations, et quand : les 7 derniers jours sous Android 13, les dernières 24 heures sous Android 12. Sceller cette étape 2. Avance autorisation par autorisation. Choisis l’autorisation qui te préoccupe — localisation, caméra, micro, agenda — et lis la chronologie des applications qui l’ont utilisée. Depuis n’importe quelle application de la liste, tu peux mettre son autorisation à jour sur-le-champ. Sceller cette étape 3. Fais-en un geste du soir, puis une décision. Sept jours (ou vingt-quatre heures) est une fenêtre glissante, pas une archive : ce que tu ne lis pas défile et se perd. Lis-le ce soir, révoque ce qui excède, et scelle les révocations — le rapport est la parole du système ; la chaîne est la tienne. Sceller cette étape Source officielle — Aide Android, Gérer les autorisations depuis le tableau de bord Confidentialité","mots":["46","ce","que","ton","telephone","raconte","ce","soir","lis","le","rapport","de","confidentialite","de","ton","propre","systeme","ton","telephone","tient","deja","le","journal","quelles","applications","ont","touche","ta","localisation","ta","camera","ou","ton","micro","et","quels","domaines","reseau","elles","ont","contactes","il","suffit","de","l","activer","et","de","le","lire","ce","guide","parcourt","les","deux","systemes","depuis","les","pages","officielles","des","fabricants","chaque","etape","se","scelle","dans","ton","cerveau","iphone","rapport","de","confidentialite","des","apps","ios","15","2","et","suivants","1","active-le","reglages","confidentialite","et","securite","rapport","de","confidentialite","des","apps","activer","il","ne","commence","a","recueillir","qu","a","partir","de","ce","moment","laisse-lui","quelques","jours","d","usage","normal","avant","de","juger","ses","donnees","sont","chiffrees","et","gardees","seulement","sur","ton","appareil","le","desactiver","les","efface","sceller","cette","etape","2","lis","les","acces","aux","capteurs","le","rapport","montre","combien","de","fois","et","quand","chaque","application","a","accede","a","des","donnees","sensibles","ou","a","des","capteurs","localisation","camera","micro","contacts","photos","au","cours","des","7","derniers","jours","une","application","qui","lit","ta","localisation","la","nuit","inutilisee","est","un","fait","sur","lequel","agir","s